WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.377
The paper's main contribution is Moccasin,

00:00:04.457 --> 00:00:08.834
a constraint programming formulation of tensor
rematerialization.

00:00:08.914 --> 00:00:13.291
Its central idea is to represent each node's
decisions as a small number of retention intervals,

00:00:13.371 --> 00:00:17.748
defined by the start and end event of the tensor's
lifetime,

00:00:17.828 --> 00:00:22.205
which reduces the count of discrete variables from
quadratic to linear in the number of nodes.

00:00:22.285 --> 00:00:26.662
On top of this,

00:00:26.742 --> 00:00:31.119
the authors show how to encode the nonlinear memory
and precedence constraints using standard CP building blocks,

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:35.576
the cumulative and reservoir constraints,

00:00:35.656 --> 00:00:40.033
and they add an optional variant that enforces an
input topological ordering to further reduce the search space.

00:00:40.113 --> 00:00:44.490
The payoff is up to an order-of-magnitude speedup
over prior work on large graphs.
